  │        Write, plan and apply GCP infrastructure          │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

  TOOLCHAIN
  ─────────
    tofu                     OpenTofu, open-source Terraform
    gcloud  gsutil  bq       Google Cloud CLI suite
    kubectl                  Kubernetes CLI
    gke-gcloud-auth-plugin   GKE cluster authentication
    k9s                      Kubernetes terminal UI
    kubectx  kubens          Switch contexts and namespaces

  TERMINAL
  ────────
    The prompt shows your git branch, tofu workspace,
    kube context and active GCP project as they change.

    k    = kubectl            tf   = tofu
    ll   = detailed listing   lt   = tree view
    z    = jump to a recent directory, e.g. z infra
    bat  = view files with syntax highlighting
    rg   = fast text search   fd   = fast file search
    Ctrl+R  search history    Ctrl+T  pick a file

  1. SIGN IN TO GOOGLE CLOUD
  ──────────────────────────
    gcloud auth login --no-launch-browser
    gcloud auth application-default login --no-launch-browser
    gcloud config set project PROJECT_ID

    The first login is for gcloud commands.
    The second one is what OpenTofu uses.

  2. FIRST OPENTOFU CONFIG
  ────────────────────────
    mkdir my-infra && cd my-infra

    cat > main.tf <<'EOF'
    terraform {
      required_providers {
        google = {
          source  = "hashicorp/google"
          version = "~> 8.0"
        }
      }
    }

    provider "google" {
      project = "PROJECT_ID"
      region  = "us-central1"
    }
    EOF

    tofu init
    tofu plan

  3. CONNECT TO A GKE CLUSTER
  ───────────────────────────
    gcloud container clusters get-credentials CLUSTER \
      --location LOCATION
    kubectl get nodes

